{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "28d32372-ea6d-84b2-b4b4-714862cc1d10",
  "created_at": "2026-02-02T11:50:24-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Julio Valdez",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:45:13-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Tony. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:45:18-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, hi Tony. Julio Valdez here. I'm calling about my water and sewer bill, and I'll tell you, it's a joke. It's a wicked high number for my shop."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:45:30-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I can take a look. What's the account under, Valdez, like you said? Is it the business or your name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:45:39-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The business, but my name's on it too. Valdez Marine Canvas. Hold on, I had the number right here. Ha, I put it down somewhere. I'm seventy-some years old, I lose my own glasses while they're on my head."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:45:55-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No rush. I can pull it up by the name if you'd rather."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:46:01-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Please do. So here's the thing. I was away six weeks. Gone. The shop was locked up, nobody in there, the water wasn't running, and the bill says I used a ton. That can't be right."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:46:16-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I've got the account up. Let me look at the readings. Yep, I see the last bill covers a long stretch, and the usage is well above what you normally run. When did you leave and when did you get back?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:46:33-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Left right after Thanksgiving, back about the middle of January. So nothing. Zero. Maybe the toilet flushed itself, I don't know."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:46:42-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, that's actually a decent thought. A running toilet or a leaky fixture in an empty building can burn through a lot of water, and the meter just counts what goes through. It could also be a bad read. Either one is possible."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:47:00-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A bad read, okay. So who fixes that? Because I'm not paying for water I didn't use. I'm a little steamed, I'll be honest."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:47:10-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. First thing, I can have the meter reading checked. Someone goes out and confirms the number on the meter matches what we billed."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:47:20-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. And before I forget, can you send me a copy of this bill? A duplicate. By email, because the paper one is all coffee-stained, Ha."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:47:31-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure can. I'll send a duplicate to the email on the account. Do you want me to confirm what we have on file?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:47:41-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, I don't trust it. Actually, you know what, just send it to what you've got and I'll tell you if it doesn't show up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:47:52-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sounds good. It should land in a little while today."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:47:57-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Now, how do I do this formally? Dispute it. I want it on paper that I'm disputing the charge, not just a phone call that goes nowhere."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:48:08-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right. So you put the dispute in writing. You send a letter or the dispute form to the billing office saying which bill, the dates, and why you think the usage is wrong, and that you were out of town. Then they hold the charge for review while the meter gets checked."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:48:29-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Whoa, slow down. Say that again slowly. I'm writing on the back of an envelope."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:48:36-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. Step one, write a letter to the billing office. Step two, put in the bill date, your account, and that you were away six weeks. Step three, ask for the meter to be rechecked and the charge held for review."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:48:53-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So, letter to billing. Bill date, account, and that I was away six weeks. And ask for the meter to be rechecked and the charge held while they review it. How's that?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:49:07-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Perfect, word for word. You could teach the class."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:49:11-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ha, don't tell my wife, she says I never listen. Okay, so what was I, oh, the meter check. Do I need to be there?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:49:22-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Probably not for the outside meter, but if it's inside the shop, somebody will need to let them in. I'll note it on the account. Is the number you're calling from the best one to reach you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:49:37-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Use the shop line. Four oh one, five five five, oh one five three."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:49:43-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, four oh one, five five five, oh one five three. I'll put in the request for a meter recheck now and note that you're disputing the bill."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:49:55-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. And in the meantime, I don't get a shutoff or some late thing, right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:50:02-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Once your written dispute is in, it's under review, and that's what protects you there. So get that letter out soon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:50:11-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'll do it this afternoon. Thanks, Tony. You were patient with an old guy."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:50:17-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Happy to help. Have a good afternoon, Mr. Valdez."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:50:21-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Bye now."
    }
  ],
